OTHER:
    --config /path/to/config    Specify a path to a custom config file
    --config none               Launch the script without a config file
    --no_config                 Don't create the user config file.
    --print_config              Print the default config file to stdout.
    --customize                 Open a menu to show/hide, reorder and rename the info lines.
                                Saving rewrites only the 'print_info()' function of the
                                config file and keeps a copy in '<config>.bak'.
                                Keys: up/down or k/j select, K/J move, space show/hide,
                                enter rename, s save, q quit.
    --stdout                    Turn off all colors and disables the ASCII logo.
    --json                      Print the information as a JSON object. Keys are the
